      "**Querying:** you embed the query, and the index walks the graph (or scans the nearest buckets) toward the closest vectors, returning the top-k with their distances — examining a tiny fraction of the data, which is why it's fast. Metadata filters narrow the candidate set, exactly or post-hoc.",
      "**Tuning:** you set parameters (graph degree, search width) to slide along the recall/latency curve. More effort per query = more accurate but slower; you pick the point your product can live with.",
