      "The alternative — brute-force comparing the query to every stored vector — is exact but **O(n)** per query; fine for a prototype with 1,000 chunks, hopeless at millions. Vector databases also add the operational glue (filtering, sharding, persistence, updates) you'd otherwise build by hand.",
